# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files — real secrets never get committed
.env*
# ...but the placeholder template MUST be, or the next person cannot know what
# the site needs. It contains no real values. The negation has to come AFTER the
# .env* line above; git evaluates last-match-wins.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# QA screenshots + agent artifacts (Audit Artifact Hygiene Rule — never committed)
/audits/
.playwright-mcp/
.optimus-review/

.vercel

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hunter Douglas confidential material — HARD BLOCK.
#
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC (github.com/tonyrosa777-ops/window-fantasies).
#
# The Hunter Douglas Business & Advertising Compliance Policy forbids a Dealer
# publishing any portion of the Policy, HD Measuring/Installation Guides, HD
# dealer cost factors, HD pricing, or dealer agreements. Committing any of it
# here would publish it to the world and is itself a compliance violation — one
# that could cost Jim the dealer locator listing this work exists to protect.
#
# The source PDFs and their transcriptions live ONLY in the sibling PRIVATE repo
# (github.com/tonyrosa777-ops/window-fantasies-docs), one directory up.
#
# What MAY live in this public repo: our own obligation strings — the marks
# table in src/data/hunterDouglas.ts and the banned-phrase list in
# scripts/hd-compliance-check.mjs. Those are our work product describing what
# OUR site must do. Never paste HD's policy prose into either one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*Media Kit*.pdf
*Media-Kit*.pdf
*Waiver Compliance Review*.pdf
hunter-douglas-media-kit.md
hunter-douglas-waiver-review.md

